  "title": "Why a Handshake or Fist Bump is Priceless",
  "summary": "A few years ago, advances in digital technology (such as smartphones, tablets, and Zoom conference calls) and the way that millennials interact and communicate (via texting and social media), gave rise to the question of whether there is a future for in-person conferences. Live events were often seen as boondoggles that could not survive in the economic and digital environment.",
